## 3. Results

## 3.1. Demographic characteristics

Patients with OCD did not exhibit significant differences from HCs in terms of age distribution and sex. However, compared to HCs, individuals with OCD showed significantly fewer years of education ( p &lt; 0.001). Furthermore, there was no notable distinction between OCD patients and HCs in mean FD ( p = 0.392). These findings are summarized in Table 1.

Table 1

Demographic and clinical characteristics.

